// PARAM: --analysis interval --solver warrow-per-origin
// Two call sites write p's FunctionEntry seed from distinct origins.
// warrow-per-origin widens each origin's own contribution and joins
// afterwards, so each site's value stays exact and the entry slot reads
// [1,2] -- enough to decide n < 10.
//
// The same program under --solver warrow is the paired known-imprecision
// case (03-warrow_joins_before_widening.vimp): widening the already-joined
// value loses the upper bound. This is the one axis on which the update-rule
// choice is observable as precision rather than only as termination.
void p(n) {
  __voblint_check(n < 10) // PROVED
}
void main() {
  p(1);
  p(2)
}
